# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (de-bridged 2026-08-16, VICE wave) ----
# VICE 3.10.0's xpet runs ON THE HOST, headless: no QEMU, no guest Debian, no
# X server, no kiosk. Frames VICE_SHM_PATH -> SH_CAPTURE=shm; keys the vicectl
# socket + the ONE shared keysym table (VICE resolves keysym -> matrix through
# PET/gtk3_buuk_sym.vkm — the BUSINESS-UK keyboard, which is this model's, not
# the graphics one pet2001 uses); audio -sounddev wav -> named FIFO with the
# daemon as clock. Launcher: the shared stations/vice-native/x11-runtime.sh.
# Build: scripts/build-guests/emulators/build-vice-native.sh cbm8032.
#
# ONE BINARY, TWO STATIONS: xpet also serves pet2001, which is why this station
# has its OWN asset tree and why SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH below names the path
# and not the binary. -model is the only runtime difference between them.
#
# THIS CONVERSION RETIRES THE WAVE'S 1600x1200 X ROOT — the biggest single
# simplification in the VICE wave. The kiosk grew its root to 1600x1200 only to
# CONTAIN VICE's fixed 1408x1064 SDL window, and streamhost then encoded all
# 1.92 Mpx of it, most of them black margin. Host-native there is no root: the
# stream is the emulated screen, 1408x1088, 36 % fewer pixels, same picture.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Commodore CBM 8032 power-on screen — "*** commodore basic 4.0 ***", "31743 bytes free" and "ready." in green on black at 80 columns, drawn double-size (-CRTCdsize) by host-native VICE 3.10.0 xpet -model 8032. PUBLISHED SURFACE 1408x1088, MEASURED off the shm mapping (6 127 680 B = 64 + 1408*1088*4) — VICE has no MAME_SHM_SIZE equivalent, the surface IS the emulated screen times CRTCDoubleSize, so this geometry follows from VICE_NATIVE_ARGS and nothing else. It replaces the bridged tile's 1600x1200 capture, which existed only to contain a fixed SDL window and encoded a black margin around it. There is no -CRTCborders: VICE's CRTC video code has no border option (asking for it is a hard parse error, not a no-op), so the border comes as the machine draws it. The scene is the machine's own untouched cold boot; nothing is curated and nothing is typed. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; PET sound -> FIFO.
VICE_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/cbm8032/vice-native/bin/xpet
VICE_NATIVE_DATA=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/cbm8032/vice-native/share/vice
# The ONLY thing that decides the published geometry (see SH_FIXTURE_DESC).
VICE_NATIVE_ARGS=-model 8032 -CRTCdsize
SH_VICECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/cbm8032/ctl.sock
SH_VICESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/cbm8032/us-layout.keysyms
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/cbm8032/audio.fifo

# ---- STANDBY (instant-ready: an emulator nobody watches costs ~0 CPU) ----
# The launcher freezes the emulator once the scene has painted; the daemon owns
# it after that (SIGSTOP after the idle grace with zero sessions, unconditional
# SIGCONT the moment a visitor connects). WITHOUT THESE TWO LINES A DE-BRIDGED
# STATION BURNS A FULL CORE AROUND THE CLOCK. _PROC_MATCH is the anti-footgun,
# and on THIS station it is load-bearing rather than defensive: pet2001 runs a
# process with the same binary NAME, so the path is the only discriminator.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/cbm8032/vice.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/cbm8032/vice-native
VICE_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING ----
# 80/80 is the VICE wave's default, established by the vic20 bisect against
# THIS engine and inherited here unchanged — the curve is a property of the
# guest's SCANNED KEYBOARD MATRIX, not of the machine's ROM. This station
# already shipped 80/80 on the bridged path, so the number does not move.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80
# No SH_KEY_MAP and no per-station keymap file: VICE's own symbolic keymap does
# that job.
